---
/**
 * ============================================================================
 * DROP ZONE COMPONENT (`DropZone.astro`)
 * ============================================================================
 * 
 * ROLE OF THIS COMPONENT:
 * Provides the interactive file ingestion target for users.
 * 
 * HOW THE HYBRID DRAG-AND-DROP / BROWSE PATTERN WORKS:
 * In modern web development, creating a great file upload experience combines
 * two mechanisms into the same visual box:
 * 
 * 1. Native File Picker:
 *    A hidden standard HTML `<input type="file" id="file-input">` is stretched to
 *    fill the entire dropzone area (`position: absolute; inset: 0; opacity: 0`).
 *    When a user clicks anywhere on the box, the browser natively opens the system
 *    file chooser dialog.
 * 
 * 2. HTML5 Drag and Drop API:
 *    When a user drags a file from their operating system desktop into the browser,
 *    JavaScript listens for `dragenter`, `dragover`, `dragleave`, and `drop` events
 *    on `#dropzone`, highlighting the border and reading the file using `FileReader`.
 * 
 * ACCESSIBILITY (a11y):
 * - `role="button"` and `tabindex="0"` allow keyboard users to tab into the dropzone
 *   and press Enter or Space to activate it.
 * - `aria-label` provides a descriptive label for screen readers.
 */
---

<section class="dropzone-section" aria-label="File Upload Dropzone">
  <div id="dropzone" class="dropzone-container" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Drop .md file here or click to browse">
    <!--
      HIDDEN FILE INPUT:
      Stretched over the container with opacity 0.
      The `accept` attribute is initialized to Markdown extensions, but `app.ts`
      dynamically updates this if the user switches tools (e.g. to Plain Text).
    -->
    <input
      type="file"
      id="file-input"
      class="file-input-hidden"
      accept=".md,.markdown"
      aria-label="File input"
    />
    
    <div class="dropzone-inner">
      <!-- Upload Cloud / Arrow SVG Icon -->
      <div class="dropzone-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path>
          <polyline points="17 8 12 3 7 8"></polyline>
          <line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="15"></line>
        </svg>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Primary Instruction -->
      <p class="dropzone-title">
        Drop your <span class="browse-highlight">.md file</span> here or click to browse
      </p>
      
      <!-- Subtitle Hint -->
      <p class="dropzone-hint">
        CommonMark & GitHub Flavored Markdown supported • Files processed strictly in memory
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
